  "lineage": "Iraqi wedding and party dance music, the country's counterpart to the Levantine dabke, built on a driving signature beat topped by crisp, rapid-fire figures on the khishba hand drum. Fiddles, double-reed shawms, oud, bass and keyboards can carry the melody, and the style is heard on Iraqi wedding and party recordings from the 1980s onward; the darbuka card stands in for the khishba.",
